-- title:
--   Rational logarithm certificates for the concrete DWZ (1,3,4) entropy rate
-- statement:
--   These are explicit rational logarithm intervals for the 134 nontrivial positive arguments needed after deterministic compatibility entropies cancel in the concrete six-region $(1,3,4)$ candidate. Each certificate records the argument, a power-of-two scale reduction, a finite-series length, and rational lower and upper logarithm bounds.
--
--   The definitions also give a finite lookup and lower and upper evaluators for $-x\log x$, valid when the coverage condition holds, as well as three rational expressions used to bound the actual coarse, joint parent-word, and compatibility-part entropies. Zero and one are handled exactly. Four deterministic compatibility parts have uncatalogued masses: their homogeneous entropy is proved to be zero directly, and the evaluator difference supplies a nonnegative conservative upper bound without assuming a logarithm interval for those masses.
--
--   Correctness of the logarithm intervals and the resulting strict entropy inequality are proved separately. No transcendental estimate is accepted on the basis of floating-point evaluation.
-- source:
